_The Computer Journal_ *27*(2), 97–111.

Programs should be written for people to read, with the order of exposition
chosen to suit the explanation rather than the compiler. The argument that
documentation belongs *in* the source, arranged for a reader, is the ancestor of
every note in this forest that explains itself.

